# Leibniz equality, the kernel's equality, on which observational equality is
# built. Two values are equal when every predicate true of one is true of the
# other, and reflexivity witnesses that every value equals itself. This is the
# bottom equality. The committed foundation extends it to observational
# equality, adding function extensionality and quotients while staying
# decidable. The integers and the reals are quotients, so the math library
# needs that extension, but every equality reduces to this core.
structure equality
  head type
  link set, like set, have type
  # Reflexivity: every value equals itself, witnessed by refl.
  assert reflexivity
    head type, have type
    have set
  # Indiscernibility: equals satisfy the same predicates. This is the
  # defining content of Leibniz equality.
  assert indiscernibility
    head type, have type
    have set
